// idem editor -- a scene editor for idem games, in `id`, drawn by idem.
//
//   tools/idem edit <gamedir>
//
// The game's sources arrive on stdin, concatenated with `#file` markers, exactly
// as `idem pack` and `idem check` receive them -- `id` has no file I/O, so a
// program that wants to see a project is handed one. They are lexed with the
// engine's own lexer, and the panes are built from the token stream: the project
// browser lists the files the markers name, and the hierarchy lists every
// declaration the lexer found.
//
// The layout is the one every 3D editor has settled on and Unity made standard:
// a menu bar, a toolbar, a hierarchy on the left, an inspector on the right, a
// project browser along the bottom, and the scene view in the middle with an
// orbit camera on the mouse. It is a familiar arrangement because it is a good
// one, and because an editor that has to be learned is an editor that is not used.
//
// The init chain is the engine's own and its order is not negotiable: an exported
// global does not exist until its declaring function has run, so trigonometry
// before anything that takes a sine, a surface before anything that measures
// itself against one, and the window before either.

// One argument of any kind means `--shot`: render frames and write the last one
// to stdout as a PPM instead of opening a loop. That is the engine's own
// verification path (ARCHITECTURE.md §10) and it needs no display at all, which
// is what lets an editor -- a program whose entire output is pixels -- be checked
// by a script.
//
// `--shot 120` runs 120 of them, which is the only way to check something that
// takes time: the game running under `play`, an animation advancing, a drag. It
// is the same shot_n the runtime uses, so the two spell it identically.
main(int argc, string[] argv) {
  ed_boot();
  ed_run(argc, argv);
} return int 0;

ed_boot() {
  fx_trig_init();
  rnd_init(20260730);
  ed_boot2();
} return void;

// 640x400 at scale 2. The window manager gets the last word on the size of the
// window and sys_present re-fits every frame, so this is a request, not a layout
// assumption -- ed_lay recomputes every rect from the surface each frame.
ed_boot2() {
  sys_open(640, 400, 2, "idem editor");
  txt_init();
  ed_boot3();
} return void;
